exports[`agent context files > writes every agent file and registers the MCP server 1`] = `
"<!-- ndop:start -->

## Ndop UI

This app uses [Ndop UI](https://ndop.dev): accessible Angular components installed as source files you own. The ndop CLI writes this section and refreshes it on \`ndop add\`; keep your own notes outside it.

### Workflow

1. Build UI from the registry. Before writing any component, layout or screen, look for it in \`npx ndop list\` (every component, and blocks for whole screens) and install what fits with \`npx ndop add <names> --yes\`. Never hand-build or copy what the registry has.
2. Before using an item, read it with \`npx ndop view <name>\`. Use its selectors, inputs and nesting exactly; never guess an API.
3. Give every form field a visible label with the \`label\` component (\`<label ndLabel>\`); a placeholder or \`aria-label\` alone is not a label.
4. Take every color, radius and font from the theme tokens below, in templates, stylesheets and inline styles alike; never write color values or define CSS variables of your own. Use logical utilities (\`ms-\`, \`pe-\`, \`start-\`, \`text-start\`), not \`ml-\`, \`pr-\`, \`left-\` or \`text-left\`.
5. Change how a component looks in its own file under \`src/app/ui\`. Don't edit \`@ndop/primitives\` or import its private paths.
6. Run \`npx ndop verify <files> --json\` on the files you changed, fix every problem it reports, and repeat until it passes. If it says \`@ndop/verify\` is missing, install it as a dev dependency first.
7. When styles, icons or a build fail in a way that points at the setup (missing tokens, providers, packages or aliases), run \`npx ndop doctor --json\`; \`npx ndop doctor --fix --yes\` applies its safe fixes.

### Installed

\`default\` 1.0.0, \`icons\` 1.0.0, \`utils\` 1.0.0.

Components are in \`src/app/ui\` (\`@/ui/…\`), helpers in \`src/app/lib\` (\`@/lib/…\`) and blocks in \`src/app/blocks\` (\`@/blocks/…\`).

### Tokens

Colors, as \`bg-*\`, \`text-*\` and \`border-*\` utilities or \`var(--name)\`: \`accent\`, \`accent-foreground\`, \`background\`, \`border\`, \`card\`, \`card-foreground\`, \`chart-1\`, \`chart-2\`, \`chart-3\`, \`chart-4\`, \`chart-5\`, \`destructive\`, \`foreground\`, \`input\`, \`muted\`, \`muted-foreground\`, \`popover\`, \`popover-foreground\`, \`primary\`, \`primary-foreground\`, \`ring\`, \`secondary\`, \`secondary-foreground\`, \`sidebar\`, \`sidebar-accent\`, \`sidebar-accent-foreground\`, \`sidebar-border\`, \`sidebar-foreground\`, \`sidebar-primary\`, \`sidebar-primary-foreground\`, \`sidebar-ring\`.

Fonts: \`font-mono\`, \`font-sans\`.

Others: \`radius\`.

### MCP server

The \`ndop\` MCP server is registered for Claude Code, Cursor and GitHub Copilot. If you have its tools, they can replace \`ndop list\` and \`ndop view\`.

<!-- ndop:end -->
"
`;

exports[`agent context files > writes every agent file and registers the MCP server 2`] = `
"<!-- ndop:start -->

## Ndop UI

This app uses [Ndop UI](https://ndop.dev): accessible Angular components installed as source files you own. The ndop CLI writes this section and refreshes it on \`ndop add\`; keep your own notes outside it.

### Workflow

1. Build UI from the registry. Before writing any component, layout or screen, look for it with the \`search_components\` and \`list_blocks\` MCP tools (blocks are whole screens) and install what fits with \`add_items\`. Never hand-build or copy what the registry has.
2. Before using an item, read it with the \`get_component\` or \`get_block\` MCP tool (if the tools are unavailable, \`npx ndop list\` and \`npx ndop view <name>\` do the same). Use its selectors, inputs and nesting exactly; never guess an API.
3. Give every form field a visible label with the \`label\` component (\`<label ndLabel>\`); a placeholder or \`aria-label\` alone is not a label.
4. Take every color, radius and font from the theme tokens below, in templates, stylesheets and inline styles alike; never write color values or define CSS variables of your own. Use logical utilities (\`ms-\`, \`pe-\`, \`start-\`, \`text-start\`), not \`ml-\`, \`pr-\`, \`left-\` or \`text-left\`.
5. Change how a component looks in its own file under \`src/app/ui\`. Don't edit \`@ndop/primitives\` or import its private paths.
6. Run \`npx ndop verify <files> --json\` on the files you changed, fix every problem it reports, and repeat until it passes. If it says \`@ndop/verify\` is missing, install it as a dev dependency first.
7. When styles, icons or a build fail in a way that points at the setup (missing tokens, providers, packages or aliases), run \`npx ndop doctor --json\`; \`npx ndop doctor --fix --yes\` applies its safe fixes.

### Installed

\`default\` 1.0.0, \`icons\` 1.0.0, \`utils\` 1.0.0.

Components are in \`src/app/ui\` (\`@/ui/…\`), helpers in \`src/app/lib\` (\`@/lib/…\`) and blocks in \`src/app/blocks\` (\`@/blocks/…\`).

### Tokens

Colors, as \`bg-*\`, \`text-*\` and \`border-*\` utilities or \`var(--name)\`: \`accent\`, \`accent-foreground\`, \`background\`, \`border\`, \`card\`, \`card-foreground\`, \`chart-1\`, \`chart-2\`, \`chart-3\`, \`chart-4\`, \`chart-5\`, \`destructive\`, \`foreground\`, \`input\`, \`muted\`, \`muted-foreground\`, \`popover\`, \`popover-foreground\`, \`primary\`, \`primary-foreground\`, \`ring\`, \`secondary\`, \`secondary-foreground\`, \`sidebar\`, \`sidebar-accent\`, \`sidebar-accent-foreground\`, \`sidebar-border\`, \`sidebar-foreground\`, \`sidebar-primary\`, \`sidebar-primary-foreground\`, \`sidebar-ring\`.

Fonts: \`font-mono\`, \`font-sans\`.

Others: \`radius\`.

<!-- ndop:end -->
"
`;
